<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBQA-F002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F002" ;
  triage:title "Duplicate compatibility DTOs with no drift guard" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-core/src/boundary/mod.rs:182,202 -- PostSendHookEventWire and ExternalPostSendHookPayload are structurally byte-identical (introduced/extended by sprint AZ.1) and legitimately kept separate per two independently-versioned compatibility windows (ADR-054), but nothing mechanically ties them together -- a future field change to PostSendHookEvent could silently desync the two byte-identical contracts AC1 depends on. Fix (either): share a private constructor helper, or add a parity test asserting serde_json::to_value equality between the two wrappers for a representative event." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "missing-drift-guard" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/boundary/mod.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
